# `wrangler pages dev .` writes its local state here. It is a scratch
# directory for the dev server and never part of a deploy.
.wrangler/

# The secrets `wrangler pages dev .` hands to the Functions locally —
# SAVE_SALT, and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET if you are driving the sign-in. The
# deployed site reads them from the Pages dashboard and this file is only
# ever the local stand-in, so it is the one file in the repo that must never
# be committed. It was not ignored for the first day Google sign-in existed.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# The pictures design/feedback/render.mjs draws of the mockups beside it. A
# picture of a page that is not built yet is not something to keep in git —
# the HTML it is drawn from is, and one command redraws the lot.
design/feedback/shots/
